<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neches River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neches River is a river of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> that flows south-east through the Piney Woods to Sabine Lake near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>. Its upper valley and that of its tributary, the Angelina, were the heartland of the Hasinai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caddo">Caddo</a>, among whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> founded its first East Texas missions in 1690.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neches-river.jpg" alt="Neches River" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William L. Farr · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Neches_River,_Orange_County,_Texas,_USA_(October_2016).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
